   "text": "This is atropine sulfate: two identical atropine units plus one sulfuric acid, written as three dot-separated fragments.\n\n**Each atropine unit**\n- A tropane core: a bicyclic system with an N-methyl bridge, with the 3-position carbon bearing the ester oxygen.\n- The ester is O\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH(CH2OH)\u2013phenyl, a tropic acid ester. Its CH is drawn with plain bonds, so it gets no stereo label.\n- The two bridgehead carbons carry explicit H wedges: the top bridgehead has its H wedged up, the bottom one has its H wedged down. I assigned @/@@ from the 2D geometry of those wedges (viewed from the H, the top bridgehead's neighbours run left, right, N clockwise; for the bottom one, N, left, right run counter-clockwise). This gives `[C@@H]2` for the top bridgehead and `[C@H]1` for the bottom one in the SMILES order used below.\n- The two units are drawn identically, so they get the same stereo labels.\n\n**Counter-acid:** S(=O)(=O)(OH)2 is written as `OS(=O)(=O)O`.\n\nSMILES: CN1[C@@H]2CC[C@H]1CC(OC(=O)C(CO)c1ccccc1)C2.CN1[C@@H]2CC[C@H]1CC(OC(=O)C(CO)c1ccccc1)C2.OS(=O)(=O)O"
